@@ -15,3 +15,29 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Account security is available at `/devtools-times/account`. Sign-up creates a local
+account with a password, followed by an optional passkey registration step. Sign-in
+supports discoverable passkeys or a password. Security settings support adding,
+renaming, and removing passkeys, with reauthentication after five minutes.
+WebAuthn challenges expire after five minutes and are single-use. Private keys and
+biometric data stay with the user's authenticator.
+
+The authentication API now runs in this app instead of the previous remote demo
+login/register service. Accounts from that demo service are not migrated.
+
+- Use HTTPS (or localhost) for WebAuthn. Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the public origin when
+  deploying behind a proxy, e.g. `https://example.com` (no path or trailing slash).
+- Account records, password hashes, and public credentials are stored in
+  `.data/accounts.json`, or the path specified by `AUTH_DATA_FILE`. Keep this file
+  on persistent private storage. Do not serve it as a static asset.
+- This sample uses a serialized file store and process-local sessions and rate
+  limits. Restarting the process signs users out. For multiple server instances,
+  replace these with a shared transactional database and shared session store.
+- Passwords remain available as a fallback, including after removing the final
+  passkey. Account recovery and migrating users from the old service are outside
+  this sample's scope.
+
+WebAuthn is implemented with [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/).
